    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSherry FitzGerald McMahon are delighted to present to market this superbly finished four-bedroom bungalow, set on an elevated 0.52-acre site in the highly sought-after Barntick area, on the outskirts of Ennis town along the Kildysart Road. The property enjoys a peaceful and secluded setting, while remaining within easy reach of Ennis town and all its amenities.\n\nInternally, the property offers bright, well-proportioned and versatile family accommodation. The accommodation comprises a welcoming entrance hall, kitchen/dining area positioned to the rear of the property and adjoining living room, complete with media wall and insert stove. A formal sitting room to the front of the property features a second insert stove and enjoys lovely views over the surrounding countryside. Four well-proportioned double bedrooms and the main bathroom complete the accommodation.\n\nExternally, the property occupies a beautifully maintained and exceptionally well-developed 0.52-acre site. A gated side entrance leads onto a sweeping tarmac driveway, providing generous off-street parking, while extensive lawn areas surround the property to the front, side and rear. The boundaries are well defined by a stone wall to the front, block wall to the side and mature hedgerow to the rear. To the rear of the property is a substantial block-built shed, which is wired and plumbed and provides excellent additional storage or potential workspace. A covered pergola area positioned between the house and shed provides an attractive and sheltered outdoor entertaining space.\n\nThis is a truly delightful property which offers excellent family accommodation, superb outdoor space and a wonderful sense of privacy in a peaceful countryside setting, while still being conveniently located close to Ennis town. \n\nViewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate all that this exceptional property has to offer."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - \nLaminate timber flooring, doors to kitchen/dining room, living room, sitting room, four bedrooms and main bathroom.\n\nKitchen Dining Room - \nTiled flooring, timber kitchen with integrated appliances, electric hob, extractor fan, plumbed for washing machine and dishwasher. Door to living room and main hallway.\n\nLiving Room - \nLaminate timber flooring, solid fuel insert stove with built in cabinates at either side of the chimney.\n\nSitting Room - \nTimber flooring, solid fuel insert stove and large front aspect window.\n\nBedroom 1 - \nLaminate timber flooring and front aspect window.\n\nBedroom 2 - \nLaminate timber flooring, built in wardrobes and shelving and front aspect window.\n\nBedroom 3 - \nLaminate timber flooring and rear aspect window.\n\nBedroom 4 - \nLaminate timber flooring, built in wardrobes and rear aspect window.\n\nBathroom - \nFully tiled throughout, WC, WHB with vanity unit, level access shower with one panel screen and electic shower, heated towel rail and rear aspect frosted window.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Four bedroom bungalow</li><li>Build 1980</li><li>Set on 0.52-acre site approx.</li><li>8 minute drive to Ennis</li><li>Fiber broadband</li><li>Landscaped Gardens</li><li>Oil fired central heating</li><li>Mains water</li><li>Septic tank on site</li><li>BER - C</ul>"
